<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guinea-Bissau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guinea-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bissau">Bissau</a> is a country on the West African coast. Part of its territory corresponds to the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a>, which emerged as an outlying province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>. It later became a Portuguese colony, and Portuguese remains its official language, part of the linguistic legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guinea-bissau.jpg" alt="Guinea-Bissau" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Guinea-Bissau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
